 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.independencia.01.ilustracion",
-  "title": "Voz pasiva: circulación de ideas ilustradas",
+  "title": "The pluperfect: what had already happened",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "Passive voice fits the spread of ideas naturally: ideas were disseminated, events were followed closely, an example was admired or feared — the reader's attention stays on the idea or event, not on naming every single person who read or reacted to it. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "content": "You know the *pluscuamperfecto* from B1 Unit 1: *había* + a past participle says that something had already happened before another moment in the past. In the history of independence, it is the tool for \"by then\": by the time of the crisis of 1808, what had already changed in the world?"
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Nuevas ideas sobre la libertad y la igualdad fueron difundidas por el mundo atlántico mediante libros y periódicos.",
-          "english": "New ideas about liberty and equality were spread across the Atlantic world through books and newspapers."
+          "spanish": "En 1810 ya se habían formado juntas en varias ciudades.",
+          "english": "By 1810, juntas had already been formed in several cities."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "La independencia de Estados Unidos y la Revolución Francesa fueron seguidas de cerca por lectores criollos educados.",
-          "english": "The independence of the United States and the French Revolution were followed closely by educated criollo readers."
+          "spanish": "Antes de 1808, muchos criollos ya habían leído libros de la Ilustración.",
+          "english": "Before 1808, many criollos had already read books of the Enlightenment."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Ese ejemplo fue admirado por algunos, pero también fue temido profundamente por muchos criollos propietarios de esclavos.",
-          "english": "That example was admired by some, but was also deeply feared by many criollo slave-owners."
+          "spanish": "Los americanos no habían elegido al nuevo rey.",
+          "english": "The Americans had not chosen the new king."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "El ejemplo haitiano fue observado con gran atención por las élites criollas de todo el continente.",
-          "english": "The Haitian example was watched with great attention by criollo elites across the continent."
+          "spanish": "Cuando llegó la noticia, la crisis ya había empezado en España.",
+          "english": "When the news arrived, the crisis had already begun in Spain."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
