 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.independencia.02.movimientos-independencia",
-  "title": "Se pasivo: los movimientos de independencia",
+  "title": "Preterite and imperfect: telling the war",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "The se-passive treats the wars of independence as a collective phenomenon: uprisings were organized, a conflict was waged, campaigns were carried out, an army was defeated — without crediting a single leader for something that was, in practice, thousands of people's doing. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "content": "You know the *preterite* and the *imperfect* from A2 Unit 22. The preterite tells what happened, step by step (*llamó*, *capturaron*); the imperfect gives the background that was true at the time (*era cura*, *eran pobres*). A war story needs both."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "En México se libró un conflicto casi ininterrumpido entre 1810 y 1821.",
