 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.razaclasepoder.01.jerarquia",
-  "title": "Se pasiva / impersonal: la sociedad de castas",
+  "title": "Impersonal se: classifying people",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "The se-passive fits classification systems well: people were classified, privileges were granted or denied, a genre became popular — all sustained social practices, not one official's single act. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "content": "You know *se* with a verb from B1 Unit 6: it says what is done without saying who does it. Here it describes how a whole society was organised. With a person as the object, the verb stays singular and takes the personal *a* (*se clasificaba a las personas*). With a thing, the verb agrees with it (*se pintaban las ropas*)."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "En la sociedad colonial se clasificaba a las personas según su origen y su ascendencia.",
-          "english": "In colonial society, people were classified according to their origin and ancestry."
+          "spanish": "Se llamaba mestizo a una persona de origen español e indígena.",
