 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.razaclasepoder.02.elites",
-  "title": "Voz pasiva: peninsulares y criollos",
+  "title": "Formal cause connectors: the Bourbon reforms",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "A before-and-after policy shift is a natural home for passive voice: offices were sold, then a policy was transformed, access was restricted, posts were reserved. The institution or the practice stays the subject across the whole narrative. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "content": "You know *debido a* and *a raíz de* from B1 Unit 6. They give a cause in formal writing and are followed by a noun, not by a verb. They are useful for the Bourbon reforms, where one decision led to the next."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Muchos cargos administrativos fueron literalmente vendidos por la corona española.",
-          "english": "Many administrative posts were literally sold by the Spanish crown."
+          "spanish": "A raíz de las reformas, el rey nombró intendentes para vigilar las provincias.",
+          "english": "As a result of the reforms, the king named intendants to watch over the provinces."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Esa situación fue transformada radicalmente por las reformas borbónicas.",
-          "english": "That situation was radically transformed by the Bourbon reforms."
+          "spanish": "Debido a los nuevos impuestos, hubo protestas en varias regiones.",
+          "english": "Because of the new taxes, there were protests in several regions."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "La venta de cargos fue restringida drásticamente.",
-          "english": "The sale of posts was drastically restricted."
+          "spanish": "Los criollos perdieron cargos debido a la llegada de más peninsulares.",
+          "english": "The criollos lost posts because of the arrival of more peninsulares."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Los puestos más importantes fueron reservados casi exclusivamente para peninsulares recién llegados.",
-          "english": "The most important posts were reserved almost exclusively for newly arrived peninsulares."
+          "spanish": "A raíz de la expulsión de los jesuitas, muchas familias se molestaron.",
+          "english": "Following the expulsion of the Jesuits, many families were upset."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "A paragraph tracing a policy reversal often needs exactly this shape: fue vendido (what used to happen) → fue transformada (the turning point) → fue restringida / fueron reservados (the new reality). Passive voice keeps the reader's attention on the practice itself changing, not on the individual officials carrying it out."
+      "content": "After *debido a* and *a raíz de* put a noun: *debido a los impuestos*. Before a verb use *porque*: *se molestaron porque perdieron cargos*. The connector can open the sentence or follow the main clause."
     }
   ]
 }
diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-razaclasepoder-03-posicion-social-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-razaclasepoder-03-posicion-social-gr.json
