 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.razaclasepoder.03.posicion-social",
-  "title": "Gerundio: posición social indígena y afrodescendiente",
+  "title": "A pesar de: despite a difficulty",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "An opening gerund can describe the motive or method behind an action (buscando proteger, buscando aprovechar) or introduce the analytical move a paragraph is making (comparando, resistiendo). These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "content": "You know *a pesar de que* and *pese a* from B1 Unit 32: they admit a difficulty and then say what happened anyway. This is a good pattern for rebellion and resistance, where people acted despite great risk. *A pesar de* + noun or infinitive, *a pesar de que* + a full clause."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Buscando en teoría 'protegerlos', la corona clasificó a los indígenas legalmente casi como menores de edad permanentes.",
-          "english": "Seeking, in theory, to 'protect' them, the crown classified indigenous people legally as almost permanent legal minors."
+          "spanish": "A pesar de las prohibiciones, los palenques sobrevivieron durante años.",
+          "english": "Despite the bans, the palenques survived for years."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Buscando aprovechar cualquier vía de movilidad disponible, muchos hombres libres se alistaron en milicias locales.",
-          "english": "Seeking to take advantage of any available path to mobility, many free men enlisted in local militias."
+          "spanish": "A pesar de que era muy peligroso, algunas personas esclavizadas huían de las haciendas.",
+          "english": "Although it was very dangerous, some enslaved people ran away from the haciendas."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Resistiendo militarmente los intentos españoles de reconquistarlo, San Basilio de Palenque logró un reconocimiento formal de su libertad.",
-          "english": "Militarily resisting Spanish attempts to reconquer it, San Basilio de Palenque achieved formal recognition of its freedom."
+          "spanish": "Pese a la derrota, el recuerdo de Túpac Amaru siguió vivo.",
+          "english": "Despite the defeat, the memory of Túpac Amaru lived on."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Comparando ambas experiencias, resulta evidente que ninguna encajaba en una sola categoría de 'oprimidos'.",
-          "english": "Comparing both experiences, it becomes clear that neither fit into a single category of 'the oppressed'."
+          "spanish": "A pesar de ser libres, muchos artesanos tenían menos derechos.",
+          "english": "Despite being free, many craftsmen had fewer rights."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Buscando + infinitive (buscando proteger, buscando aprovechar) is a common way to state a goal or intention behind an action — it answers \"with what aim?\" the same way an opening gerund usually answers \"how?\" or \"while doing what?\""
+      "content": "*A pesar de* is followed by a noun or an infinitive (*a pesar de ser libres*). Before a full clause use *a pesar de que* with the indicative when the fact is real (*a pesar de que era peligroso*)."
     }
   ]
 }
diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-razaclasepoder-04-mestizaje-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-razaclasepoder-04-mestizaje-gr.json
