   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "*A lo largo de* tracks a demographic trend across time; *a raíz de* and como consecuencia de both draw out what followed from that trend. Used together, they let a paragraph move from 'this kept happening' to 'and because of that, the system had to respond'. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "content": "You know *es importante que*, *es necesario que* and *es mejor que* + the present subjunctive from A2 Unit 27: a judgement about what should happen takes the subjunctive. Here they give what officials, the elite or historians think. Keep the main clause in the present: it is a view, not a past event."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "A lo largo del periodo colonial, la mezcla entre poblaciones avanzó de forma constante.",
-          "english": "Throughout the colonial period, mixing between populations advanced steadily."
+          "spanish": "Para los funcionarios es importante que cada persona tenga un lugar en la lista.",
+          "english": "For the officials it is important that each person has a place on the list."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "A raíz de esta realidad demográfica, el sistema legal de castas se volvió cada vez más difícil de sostener.",
-          "english": "As a result of this demographic reality, the legal caste system became increasingly hard to sustain."
+          "spanish": "Es necesario que el registro diga el origen de la familia.",
+          "english": "It is necessary that the register states the family's origin."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Como consecuencia de esa tensión, la corona terminó recurriendo a una solución tan insólita como reveladora.",
-          "english": "As a consequence of that tension, the crown ended up resorting to a solution as unusual as it was revealing."
+          "spanish": "Para la élite es mejor que las categorías no cambien.",
+          "english": "For the elite it is better that the categories do not change."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "A lo largo de estas últimas décadas coloniales, la desigualdad no disminuyó a pesar del aumento de la mezcla.",
-          "english": "Throughout these final colonial decades, inequality didn't decrease despite the increase in mixing."
+          "spanish": "Para muchos historiadores es importante que hoy se estudie esta historia.",
+          "english": "For many historians it is important that this history is studied today."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Notice *a lo largo de* opens and closes this whole argument (colonial period... final colonial decades) while *a raíz de* / como consecuencia de sit in the middle, marking the turning points. That's a common shape for a formal historical paragraph: time-span, cause, time-span again."
+      "content": "The verb after *que* is in the present subjunctive (*tenga*, *diga*, *cambien*, *se estudie*). If nobody in particular is meant, use the infinitive instead: *es importante estudiar esta historia*."
